From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Favre <ben@webdesign29.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:55:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clipper: initialise polygon node join and end types

Why: copying a newly constructed PolyNode during polygon union reads uninitialised enum members. UBSan detects an invalid EndType while arranging a wipe tower. Initialise both enums before any node or tree copy.

Files: src/clipper/clipper.hpp. Upstreamable: yes; removes undefined behaviour in Clipper polygon ownership independently of the facade.

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 src/clipper/clipper.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/clipper/clipper.hpp b/src/clipper/clipper.hpp
index b1dae3c..edff8f3 100644
--- a/src/clipper/clipper.hpp
+++ b/src/clipper/clipper.hpp
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ typedef std::vector< PolyNode* > PolyNodes;
 class PolyNode 
 { 
 public:
-    PolyNode() : Childs(), Parent(0), Index(0), m_IsOpen(false) {}
+    PolyNode() : Childs(), Parent(0), Index(0), m_IsOpen(false), m_jointype(jtSquare), m_endtype(etClosedPolygon) {}
     virtual ~PolyNode(){};
     Path Contour;
     PolyNodes Childs;
